The proxymacs Emacs package simplifies HTTP, HTTPS, and SOCKS proxy configuration. It supports HTTP/HTTPS proxies and SOCKS4, SOCKS4a, and SOCKS5. Note: If this project helps your workflow, please consider supporting the project by ⭐ starring it on GitHub and sharing it on your website, blog, Mastodon, Reddit, X, LinkedIn, or other social media platforms so other Emacs users can discover its benefits. Usage HTTP and HTTPS Proxy (setq proxymacs-proxy-type 'http) (setq proxymacs-http-host &#34;127.0.0.1&#34;) (setq proxymacs-http-port 3128) ; accepts integer or string (setq proxymacs-http-no-proxy &#34;^\\(localhost\\&#124;127\\.0\\.0\\.1\\&#124;10\\..*\\&#124;192\\.168\\..*\\)&#34;) ;; Optional HTTPS configuration (falls back to HTTP host and port when nil): ;; (setq proxymacs-https-host &#8230; <a href="https://www.jamescherti.com/proxymacs-el/">Continue reading <span class="meta-nav">&#8594;</span></a>